---
// File role: Public-facing guide to the archive, its reading tools, Basta, saved/offline access, and Recitation Sets.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/about.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Guide | Kalam Archive"
  description="Discover Kalam Archive, learn how to search, read Urdu and Roman Urdu, explore Basta, save pages offline, and build Recitation Sets."
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <header class="page-header-simple">
      <p class="eyebrow">Kalam Archive</p>
      <h1>About &amp; contact</h1>
      <p>Preserving Urdu kalam and making it easier to find, read, and recite.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-intro about-bilingual">
      <section class="about-language" lang="en" dir="ltr" aria-labelledby="about-en-heading">
        <h2 id="about-en-heading">About the archive</h2>
        <p>
          Kalam Archive brings together Urdu nohas, salams, marsiyas, manqabats, and other
          kalam. Read Urdu alongside Roman Urdu where available, and choose the fonts,
          colours, and line spacing that suit you.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="about-language" lang="ur" dir="rtl" aria-labelledby="about-ur-heading">
        <h2 id="about-ur-heading">اس ذخیرے کے بارے میں</h2>
        <p>
          کلام آرکائیو میں اردو نوحے، سلام، مرثیے، منقبتیں اور دوسرے کلام یکجا کیے گئے ہیں۔
          جہاں دستیاب ہو، اردو کے ساتھ رومن اردو بھی پڑھ سکتے ہیں۔ مطالعے کے لیے خط،
          رنگ اور سطروں کا فاصلہ اپنی سہولت کے مطابق بدل سکتے ہیں۔
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <nav class="about-contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="about-contents-title">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#purpose">Our purpose</a></li>
        <li><a href="#discover">Browse &amp; search</a></li>
        <li><a href="#reading">Reading tools</a></li>
        <li><a href="#basta">Basta archive</a></li>
        <li><a href="#saved">Saved &amp; offline</a></li>
        <li><a href="#recitations">Recitation Sets</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Corrections &amp; contact</a></li>
        <li><a href="#support">Keep it free</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <section id="purpose" class="about-guide-section about-purpose" aria-labelledby="purpose-heading">
      <div class="about-guide-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our purpose</p>
        <h2 id="purpose-heading">A practical home for kalam</h2>
        <p>
          The aim is simple: make kalam easier to preserve, discover, read, and use in a
          majlis. The archive brings together individual lyrics and the original Basta
          book, with tools built for readers, reciters, and anjumans.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-principles">
        <div><strong>Preserve the source</strong><p>Keep original Basta page scans available alongside transcriptions so readings can be checked.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Read your way</strong><p>Choose scripts, layouts, fonts, colours, and a distraction-free reading view.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Put kalam to use</strong><p>Save useful material and assemble shareable programmes without needing an account.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="discover" class="about-guide-section" aria-labelledby="discover-heading">
      <div class="about-guide-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 · Discover</p>
        <h2 id="discover-heading">Find the kalam you need</h2>
        <p>Browse by category, look up a phrase, or narrow a search using the details attached to each kalam.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-feature-grid">
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Browse by Kalam Type</h3>
          <p>Explore nohas, salams, marsiyas, manqabats, and other types across the archive, including Basta entries.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open <a href="/">Browse</a> from the main navigation.</li>
            <li>Select a Kalam Type to view matching entries.</li>
            <li>Open a kalam to read it or add it to a recitation programme.</li>
          </ol>
          <a class="about-feature-link" href="/">Browse categories <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Search Urdu and Roman Urdu</h3>
          <p>Search titles and poem text in either script, even when you only remember a line or part of a phrase.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Type a phrase in the <a href="/search/">Search</a> page or the homepage search box.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Search in</strong> to choose Lyrics, Basta, or both.</li>
            <li>Refine with Kalam Type, Haal, tags, language, occasion, poet, or reciter; clear filters when needed.</li>
          </ol>
          <a class="about-feature-link" href="/search/">Open advanced search <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Explore credits and metadata</h3>
          <p>Where recorded, each lyric can show the poet, reciter, occasion, Haal, language, and Kalam Type.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>On a lyric page, open <strong>About this kalam</strong>.</li>
            <li>Select a linked poet, reciter, type, or other field to find related kalam.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Share individual kalams</h3>
          <p>Individual lyric and verified Basta kalam pages have their own URLs, so you can send someone directly to a poem rather than a long list.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open the kalam you want to share.</li>
            <li>Copy its page URL from your browser and send it to the reader.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="reading" class="about-guide-section" aria-labelledby="reading-heading">
      <div class="about-guide-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 · Read</p>
        <h2 id="reading-heading">Make every reading view your own</h2>
        <p>The same core reader controls work across standalone lyrics, Basta, and Recitation Sets, with options depending on what the source contains.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-feature-grid">
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Urdu, Roman Urdu, and original images</h3>
          <p>Read Urdu and Roman Urdu together or separately. Basta also offers the original scan wherever one is available.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open a poem or a Basta page and find the reading toolbar.</li>
            <li>Open <strong>View</strong> if the options are collapsed, then use <strong>Show</strong> to select Urdu, Roman, or Image.</li>
            <li>On wider screens, editions can appear alongside each other; on narrower screens, they stack.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="about-feature-note">Only editions actually available for that source are offered.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Resize bilingual text and adjust spacing</h3>
          <p>Parallel Urdu and Roman text share a reading area, with verse sizing designed to fit the available width.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>When two text columns appear side by side, drag the divider to give one more room.</li>
            <li>Choose <strong>Compact</strong>, <strong>Default</strong>, or <strong>Relaxed</strong> under <strong>Line Spacing</strong>.</li>
            <li>The text layout adapts as the available width changes.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Focus Mode and fullscreen reading</h3>
          <p>Remove surrounding distractions for a majlis, public recitation, or sustained reading session.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Focus Mode</strong> in the reading toolbar.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Options</strong> to change editions or spacing, and <strong>Browser fullscreen</strong> when desired.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Exit</strong> to return to the regular page without losing your place.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Themes, custom colours, and fonts</h3>
          <p>Choose from light, dark, sepia, AMOLED, and other reading palettes, or create your own. Urdu and Roman fonts can be selected separately.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Use the palette-shaped <strong>Appearance settings</strong> button in the site header.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Colors</strong>, select a theme or start a Custom palette and adjust its colours.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Fonts</strong>, choose the Urdu and English/Roman Urdu faces and preview them.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="about-feature-note">Appearance choices save automatically on this device. Some optional fonts require installation.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="basta" class="about-guide-section" aria-labelledby="basta-heading">
      <div class="about-guide-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 · Preserve &amp; explore</p>
        <h2 id="basta-heading">The complete Basta book archive</h2>
        <p>Read the original printed pages and their transcriptions together, or open verified poems as complete individual kalams.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-feature-grid">
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Read page by page</h3>
          <p>See an original page scan next to Urdu text and Roman Urdu where available.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>From <a href="/basta/">Basta</a>, choose <strong>Page by page</strong>.</li>
            <li>Use the Previous/Next navigation or enter a printed page number to jump directly.</li>
            <li>Select a scan to enlarge it for closer reading.</li>
          </ol>
          <a class="about-feature-link" href="/basta/">Open Basta <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Read continuously</h3>
          <p>Move through multiple printed pages as one reading session without opening each page separately.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Choose <a href="/basta/read/">Continuous reader</a> on the Basta landing page.</li>
            <li>Select visible editions, navigate with page controls or Contents, and use Focus Mode if helpful.</li>
            <li>Return later using your locally saved reading progress.</li>
          </ol>
          <a class="about-feature-link" href="/basta/read/">Open continuous reader <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Printed index and individual kalams</h3>
          <p>Find a work using its place in the original book, or read a verified complete kalam spanning several pages.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open the <a href="/basta/index/">printed index</a> or <a href="/basta/kalams/">individual kalam list</a>.</li>
            <li>Select an entry. Verified poems open in their own reader; entries under review lead to their source pages.</li>
            <li>On a multi-page individual kalam, use scan <strong>Previous</strong>/<strong>Next</strong> to compare the relevant source pages.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Check sources and download the book</h3>
          <p>Read against the original printed page, inspect the source of numbered stanzas, or keep a copy of the book.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>On an individual Basta kalam, open <strong>Source scans for numbered stanzas</strong> to locate printed sources.</li>
            <li>Select a page image for the full-size scan.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Download PDF</strong> on <a href="/basta/">Basta</a> for the complete original book.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="saved" class="about-guide-section" aria-labelledby="saved-heading">
      <div class="about-guide-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 · Keep your place</p>
        <h2 id="saved-heading">Save, resume, and read offline</h2>
        <p>Keep track of the kalams and pages you use regularly, with your personal library stored in this browser.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-feature-grid">
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Favorites, bookmarks, and reading history</h3>
          <p>Save standalone lyrics, individual Basta kalams, printed pages, and selected Basta stanzas.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Use the save or bookmark control on a lyric, Basta page, individual kalam, or numbered stanza.</li>
            <li>Open <a href="/saved/">Saved &amp; recent</a> to revisit your selections and recently viewed lyrics.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Continue reading</strong> to resume Basta when a saved position exists.</li>
          </ol>
          <a class="about-feature-link" href="/saved/">Open your library <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Save material for offline reading</h3>
          <p>Download selected archive pages for times when the internet is unreliable or unavailable.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open <a href="/saved/">Saved &amp; recent</a>, then <strong>Backup and offline reading</strong>.</li>
            <li>Choose <strong>Save bookmarked pages offline</strong>; optionally include original Basta scans.</li>
            <li>For wider preparation, download the offline search index or save a specific Basta page range.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="about-feature-note">Offline copies need to be downloaded while online and remain subject to browser storage and device limitations.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Back up and transfer your library</h3>
          <p>Move saved items, reading positions, preferences, and local Recitation Set drafts between browsers or devices.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>In <a href="/saved/">Saved &amp; recent</a>, select <strong>Export JSON backup</strong>.</li>
            <li>Keep the downloaded file somewhere secure.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Import backup</strong> on the new browser or device to restore it.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="about-feature-note">A backup may contain private organizer links for published programmes. Do not share it publicly.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>No account needed</h3>
          <p>Saved favorites, recent reading history, themes, bookmarks, and unpublished programme drafts live in your browser. Clearing browser data can erase them, so export a backup if you need to keep them.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="recitations" class="about-guide-section" aria-labelledby="recitations-heading">
      <div class="about-guide-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 · Recite together</p>
        <h2 id="recitations-heading">Plan and share Recitation Sets</h2>
        <p>Build a majlis programme from the archive, arrange it in recitation order, and give your group one reader link.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-feature-grid">
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Create a programme or use a template</h3>
          <p>Make your own sequence of up to 40 entries, or start with a reusable programme template.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open <a href="/recite/">Recitation Sets</a> and choose <strong>New set</strong> or <strong>Start from template</strong>.</li>
            <li>Add a title and, if useful, an occasion and description.</li>
            <li>Find kalam using the built-in Urdu/Roman title search, or use <strong>Add to set</strong> on a lyric page.</li>
          </ol>
          <a class="about-feature-link" href="/recite/">Build a Recitation Set <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Arrange the order and assign reciters</h3>
          <p>Adjust the programme for your gathering rather than changing the source poems.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Drag entries into order or use their arrow buttons.</li>
            <li>Add reciter assignments and notes, or repeat a kalam when needed.</li>
            <li>Keep separate local drafts and duplicate a set to adapt it for another occasion.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Customize Marsiya stanzas</h3>
          <p>For supported, verified numbered Basta Marsiyas, build the exact stanza sequence needed for a recitation.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open the stanza-arrangement controls for that Marsiya in your programme.</li>
            <li>Reorder or repeat stanzas, or borrow one from another verified Marsiya.</li>
            <li>Restore the original sequence if needed. The archive's source text remains unchanged.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Publish a link or share a QR code</h3>
          <p>Let others read the programme without giving them permission to edit it.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>When ready, select <strong>Publish set</strong>.</li>
            <li>Share the <strong>read-only public link</strong> or display its QR code.</li>
            <li>Keep the separate <strong>private organizer link</strong> secure: it allows changes and deletion.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="about-feature-note">Published links normally expire two years after the last authorized update; the organizer can choose to keep a programme available until deleted.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Guide the gathering live</h3>
          <p>Move participating readers through the same programme while allowing each person to choose whether to follow.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Use the organizer controls to <strong>Start live</strong> and advance through kalams.</li>
            <li>Readers can choose <strong>Follow organizer live</strong> or navigate independently.</li>
            <li>Stop live following when the coordinated part ends; an internet connection is required for live updates.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <h3>Read, print, or export your programme</h3>
          <p>Use the same readable Urdu/Roman layout for the whole programme, on screen or on paper.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open <strong>Read set</strong> and choose <strong>Continuous</strong> or <strong>One at a time</strong>.</li>
            <li>Use the reading toolbar and Focus Mode as needed.</li>
            <li>Open <strong>Offline reading &amp; printing</strong> to save a self-contained HTML reading copy or print/save as PDF.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="about-feature-note">Offline HTML includes text and programme details, not original page scans or live following.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="about-guide-section about-contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <div class="about-guide-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Corrections &amp; contributions</p>
        <h2 id="contact-heading">Help keep the archive accurate</h2>
        <p>
          Transcriptions and metadata are improved as errors are found. Original Basta scans
          make comparison possible, but some entries may still have mistakes, missing Roman
          text, or incomplete credits. If you notice an issue, your correction is welcome.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-contact-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Suggest a correction</h3>
          <p>Use <strong>Suggest correction</strong> on a lyric or Basta kalam page, or email us with the page URL, the relevant verse, and your proposed correction.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Contribute kalam or information</h3>
          <p>Share missing kalam, source images, accurate transcriptions, poet or reciter details, or suggestions for improving the archive.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a class="about-contact-email" href="mailto:lyricsadmin@gmail.com">
        <span>Contact the archive</span>
        <strong>lyricsadmin@gmail.com</strong>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section id="support" class="about-guide-section about-support" aria-labelledby="support-heading">
      <div class="about-support-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Keep Kalam Archive accessible</p>
        <h2 id="support-heading">Free and ad-free. Always.</h2>
        <p>
          Kalam Archive is free to use and will remain ad-free. Reading kalam, searching the
          archive, viewing original pages, and preparing recitation programmes should not
          come with advertisements or a paywall.
        </p>
        <p>
          Keeping the website online still has costs, including hosting and storage for
          original scans. If you would like to help cover those ongoing costs and keep the
          archive available to everyone, please get in touch about contributing.
        </p>
        <a class="about-support-action" href="mailto:lyricsadmin@gmail.com?subject=Supporting%20Kalam%20Archive">
          Contribute to running costs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
